-- ============================================================================
-- 31 - Dutch (nl_NL)
-- ============================================================================
-- Generated from one table keyed on the English source, so every language says
-- the same thing and a wording change to the source is a one-line edit in one
-- place rather than seven.
--
-- NO `IN Ledger` SCOPE, deliberately. The navigation menu is a project-level
-- document, not a module one, so `in Ledger` silently misses every menu
-- caption: the chart text switched language and the sidebar did not. Unscoped
-- plus `or modify` sets each source string wherever it occurs and leaves the
-- rest alone.
--
-- `create or modify` rather than `create or replace`: it MERGES. Mendix already
-- ships translations for the Atlas and System strings this app inherits — grid
-- pagination, combo-box accessibility text, the selection announcements — and
-- `or replace` would treat this file as authoritative and delete every one of
-- them. What this file names, it sets; what it does not name, it leaves.
--
-- WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT TRANSLATED. Pure placeholders and symbols ('{1}',
-- '€ {1}', the sort arrows), the seeded merchant names, and 'CSV'. A
-- translation table that maps 'Albert Heijn' to something is not localisation,
-- it is corrupting the demo data through the caption layer.
--
-- Placeholders survive verbatim. Mendix substitutes on {1} and {2}
-- positionally, so the tokens are carried through untouched even where the
-- surrounding word order changes — which it does: French and Spanish put the
-- euro sign after the number, and the table reflects that rather than
-- transliterating the English.
--
-- This covers Ledger's own UI. It is not a complete localisation of every
-- string the app can render: CheckCompleteness is left off in
-- 30-languages.mdl for exactly that reason, and anything untranslated falls
-- back to en_US.
-- ============================================================================

create or modify translations for nl_NL (
    'A row per year, a column per week, a cell per day. Dark cells are heavy days; the empty ones are days nothing was spent at all.' as 'Een rij per jaar, een kolom per week, een cel per dag. Donkere cellen zijn zware dagen; de lege zijn dagen waarop niets is uitgegeven.',
